1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,198
Hollis Ford. Forty-one people. One well.

2
00:00:04,798 --> 00:00:07,568
Since day one, everyone drinks from it.

3
00:00:08,168 --> 00:00:13,605
If six people get sick on the same morning, don't look for a bite. Look at what they drank.

4
00:00:14,205 --> 00:00:20,349
The Well. Part one of three. Six sick.

5
00:00:20,949 --> 00:00:26,127
Nell Varga tested water for the county. Now she tests it for everyone.

6
00:00:26,727 --> 00:00:29,343
Sick ones stay in the barn. Nobody opens it.

7
00:00:30,147 --> 00:00:33,398
Fever. Cramps. No bite marks.

8
00:00:33,698 --> 00:00:35,464
Then it isn't them. It's us.

9
00:00:36,064 --> 00:00:40,484
A bite hits one person. Bad water hits everyone at once.

10
00:00:41,084 --> 00:00:42,787
Panic kills faster than thirst.

11
00:00:43,087 --> 00:00:43,857
So does cholera.

12
00:00:45,584 --> 00:00:47,191
The strip does not lie.

13
00:00:48,824 --> 00:00:54,149
Forty-one people. Three liters each. One hundred twenty-three liters a day.

14
00:00:54,749 --> 00:00:55,759
Do not drink that.

15
00:00:57,449 --> 00:00:59,209
Someone opened this well last night.

16
00:01:00,509 --> 00:01:02,370
I'm sorry. T.

17
00:01:03,569 --> 00:01:07,931
Part one of three, The Well. Next: the boiling point.
